[[- define "json-only" -]]
Return only the JSON object: no code fence, no commentary before or after it. Every value is a string, except "tags", which is an array of strings.
[[- end]]

[[- define "field-ownership" -]]
## Field Ownership

- "name": the character's or scenario's name
- "description": character role, appearance, behavior-relevant backstory only
- "personality": persistent drives, speech style, limits, likes/dislikes
- "scenario": current situation and immediate stakes
- "first_mes": the opening roleplay message
- "mes_example": example dialogue blocks (preserve <START> tag formatting exactly)
- "system_prompt": OOC behavioral contract and rules
- "post_history_instructions": per-turn format and enforcement
- "creator_notes": notes for the player, such as credits, intended play style, and boundaries. Apps show it but don't send it to the model, so its length costs no tokens and rules for the AI written here never reach it
- "tags": a list of short tags
[[- end]]
